<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Bash</h1>
<p>Skill
Class: Fighter (guild level 0), Dark Knight (guild level 3, up to 80%), Paladin (guild level 3, up to 80%), Ranger (guild level 3, up to 80%), Druid (guild level 23, up to 50%)
Also taught by: Gustav, in the back room of the inn in Udgaard (anyone, up to 35%); an old sinewy man, in a sea cave in the Fjord (once you have brought him food)
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>bash &lt;character&gt;
bash               (in a fight: your opponent)
</pre>
<p>Bash your opponent with your shield, improving your chance of winning, if you're good that is. A bash that lands in a fight knocks your opponent off balance, so that they lose a round; and once bashed, they can't be bashed again for a few rounds.
</p><p>You must wear a shield. Your bash skill and strength are set against your opponent's dexterity (and a player's own bash skill). If you miss, you bash the passing wind and lose half a round; miss badly and your shield slips from your arm, and you lose a whole round. You can't bash someone who isn't standing, or who is much heavier than you: the stronger, heavier and more skilled you are, the bigger the creatures you can bash. Each try costs 10 endurance.
</p><p>Bashing starts a fight if there isn't one. You can bash another player only when both of you have signed the Book of Blood. Practising it needs strength 10.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Shields</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Kick</a>
</pre>




</div>